{"title":"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(For_Educated_Guessing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (For Educated Guessing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/882b0bc0d2adb26b91473a0630691f8dba25fb69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 25$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078eeaa7c8398d4f1a83f68c101488e5e7d946fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 39$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff00b88cc7d3038b45fd91617f570dda6f3e5b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> respectively, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e755d945f894be6dfbf3710aa6c907f34aa82c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa660e1d804adc33b5f2613d6da4da956708e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. What is the ratio of the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> to the area of the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c493dd2882ca1eb621281106a4d91bd73e092e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1c2fa9191e2b2d5f5201b98432d9ef50640fc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{266}{1521}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{19}{75}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{19}{56}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"417\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7f72303ecda76e14992764cd8189ea495884ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{AD}{AB} \\cdot \\frac{AE}{AC} = \\frac{19}{25} \\cdot \\frac{14}{42} = \\frac{19}{75}.\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>(Area of a triangle is half times base times height, so the area ratio of triangles, that have a common vertex (height) and bases on a common line, is the base length ratio. This is applied twice, using different pairs of bases, and corresponding altitudes for height.).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2fdc4687b12e3806e8997a889e00dce6eb1d06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.15 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E;  A = (191/39,28*sqrt(1166)/39); B = (0,0); C = (39,0); D = (6*A + 19*B)/25; E = (28*A + 14*C)/42;  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, NE); label(&quot;$19$&quot;, (A + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (B + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$14$&quot;, (A + E)/2, NE); label(&quot;$28$&quot;, (C + E)/2, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55eb2fcfbad02e393d8d58681100faa707370dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BCED] = [ABC] - [ADE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82ada7b0f131d9c26a53ef4d0ef37be11d728841.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{[ADE]}{[BCED]} &amp;= \\frac{[ADE]}{[ABC] - [ADE]} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\frac{ABC}{ADE} - 1} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\frac{75}{19} - 1} \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{19}{56}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"226\" height=\"197\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: If it is hard to understand why <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36d273ebd006b209b3b800f87eddc9e62da0b740.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{AD}{AB} \\cdot \\frac{AE}{AC}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" />, you can use the fact that the area of a triangle equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aaddf799a9629a146c12d5677528ade397047727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot ab \\cdot \\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />. If angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1642ca9ca4437b86ff39016b73db9b8bef72ed8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAE = Z$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549d9a4c9b836beb92b88f749b9525aeebcf90f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 19 \\cdot 14 \\cdot \\sin(Z)}{\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 25 \\cdot 42 \\cdot \\sin(Z)} = \\frac{19 \\cdot 14}{25 \\cdot 42} = \\frac{ab}{cd}\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VXyOJWcpi00\">https://youtu.be/VXyOJWcpi00</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2fdc4687b12e3806e8997a889e00dce6eb1d06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.15 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E;  A = (191/39,28*sqrt(1166)/39); B = (0,0); C = (39,0); D = (6*A + 19*B)/25; E = (28*A + 14*C)/42;  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, NE); label(&quot;$19$&quot;, (A + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (B + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$14$&quot;, (A + E)/2, NE); label(&quot;$28$&quot;, (C + E)/2, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86ba9d0f9872cdff2d46a43976bf40ce4791b085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADE]=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3fa23548a4043fd54c657bccb2799dd8aa53ea80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=2 \\cdot EA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed506e1c7e90802b10f9d576f89e6c365613cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEC]=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. \nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c0ca9888c6b3c0bbdb6c99a6bf4b6e90d9d516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADC]=3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. \nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef0842baed8c152e7b5af87b8ea841df0fe203a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BDC]=\\frac{6}{19}\\cdot3x=\\frac{18x}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" />. \nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce3cc9f87e1dab7e76878face9c746da1d71fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[ADE]}{[BCED]} = \\frac{x}{\\frac{18x}{19}+2x}= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{19}{56}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"268\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>-Conantwiz2023\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(trig)\">Solution 3 (trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da429ed8ef13911ee18125c103294e932cfb5aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} bc\\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Using this formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/4994450bce1d1f4bb79c88144f39f85e954923c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADE]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot19\\cdot14\\cdot\\sin A = 133\\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"299\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d54255e8dd4f8c76b2fe7fb3a02cc6a1a7bd0dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot25\\cdot42\\cdot\\sin A = 525\\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"298\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c493dd2882ca1eb621281106a4d91bd73e092e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> minus the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238b4f47585fadb1facd70b51395692d972ba99d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BCED] = 525\\sin A - 133\\sin A = 392\\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the desired ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94cde4e7a72e75bda336d247702077b572e4e19a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{133\\sin A}{392\\sin A}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{19}{56}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"169\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55ff2cc3abd7b0aeed47eb38b12999e3d3d0881c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=39$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> was not used in this solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/308be5f58bde91ac93689cb9ca6c261cb896e02e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE\\parallel BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" /> then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4b550af96bcf412d6e4bbed2f53699ee354731.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[ABF]}=\\left(\\frac{AD}{AB}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{19}{25}\\right)^2=\\frac{361}{625}\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/a/6ea4aca76698ef059a9ba2fae077bf072feea811.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[DEFB]}=\\frac{361}{625-361}=\\frac{361}{364}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d0193044bd751122e1a1617caf84aa0de51782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ADE\\sim\\bigtriangleup ABF$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce6e1033d3a0dcef6a33ea9f696596d76ed473b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AD}{AE}=\\frac{DB}{EF}\\Longrightarrow EF=\\frac{84}{19}\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba73cba82fa4657f04aeda4ef2734e241270fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FC=EC-EF=\\frac{448}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b97c0c0136cdc28188c625cb0eb6514e18361cf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ABF]}{[BFC]}=\\frac{AF}{FC}=\\frac{350}{448}\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8f8cd8c3e17b7356836be174bbd276adb168ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[BFC]}=\\left(\\frac{[ADE]}{[ABF]}\\right)\\left(\\frac{[ABF]}{[BFC]}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{361}{625}\\right)\\left(\\frac{350}{448}\\right)=\\frac{126350}{280000}\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"43\" />\nFinally, after some calculations,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706cb9247b37c8c2586243483b2f19c93bde3d41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ADE]}{[DECB]}=\\frac{[ADE]}{[BFC]+[DECB]}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) \\ } \\frac{19}{56}}\\]\" width=\"344\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p><p>~ LaTeX changes by tkfun\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the area of triangle ABC be denoted by [ABC] and the area of quadrilateral ABCD be denoted by [ABCD].\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d7815ebabb0759e1f0a200bddf335d4c3bbf6ece.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Diagram:}\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2fdc4687b12e3806e8997a889e00dce6eb1d06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.15 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E;  A = (191/39,28*sqrt(1166)/39); B = (0,0); C = (39,0); D = (6*A + 19*B)/25; E = (28*A + 14*C)/42;  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, NE); label(&quot;$19$&quot;, (A + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (B + D)/2, W); label(&quot;$14$&quot;, (A + E)/2, NE); label(&quot;$28$&quot;, (C + E)/2, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p>Let the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> share a height, and the ratio of their bases are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e1a1a7adf986532b7598e896785a56c785f779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3fc48324430ab8e4592260bcaccc655503255f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"16\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c45c55274427f284efb69f46e4c5917a5ae7f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> share a height, and the ratio of their bases is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69200bb2044e60f19e43a427a43b54993acac696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19:6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, so the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0ef9ca648553421646fa1df3ae9c6ff0f7fe28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[AED]}{[AEB]}=\\frac{19}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"45\" />. Therefore, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb60f5a44cea29d033604bedca7fec8a0f74f22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[AED]=\\frac{19}{25}\\cdot\\left[AEB\\right]=\\frac{19}{25}\\cdot\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\left[ABC\\right]=\\frac{19}{25}\\cdot\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot x=\\frac{19}{75}x\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da23782dbb557b27be433d37719ebdbd4b72784.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[DECB]=[ABC]-[AED]=x-\\frac{19}{75}x=\\frac{56}{75}x\\]\" width=\"365\" height=\"38\" />\nThe ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafb167f0920f7d4bd1271f715cb24b95bacf699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[AED]}{[DECB]}=\\frac{\\frac{19}{75}}{\\frac{56}{75}}=\\frac{19}{56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"167\" height=\"49\" /> which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f76960cfe45dca5b2cbdf060c1b959105ed26f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{19}{56}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is 478. Scale everything by 39. The height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba15d20d7fa78a0b40dd8b814b8e9d07278ea29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = 956$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n<span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2005_amc_10a_q25.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d8/2005_amc_10a_q25.png/450px-2005_amc_10a_q25.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"315\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d8/2005_amc_10a_q25.png/675px-2005_amc_10a_q25.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d8/2005_amc_10a_q25.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd1ca98e626c085660123908b1f8895269cfe68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/072423a9f3685d8fb0b9ec184efd28b8b74f9798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(1521,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f87a77acb1a4571efdea4e0dbe012a31a27106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX; x = 191$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1d7351a9a0aad6a531d6545ed35fc4dbc0be69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = 191$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c192d920db7de57181972a7cf2f0bb0e530dcece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = 1330$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. So, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac2bb2fa92990b458b63aecfcc40d592583e2a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAX = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07ffff275d6c910031ac57b24ba32cd707b67bd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAX = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f3ba7357a0476b83cb43fddc7869d08d37892b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\alpha) = \\frac{119}{975}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5434baaccfbc7f2676cffe96d6c744813fa943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\beta) = \\frac{1330}{1638} = \\frac{95}{117}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a123a1ec4e3c3ca83080e3cc6083d48314f08fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\alpha) = \\frac{956}{975}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b3c706852b63735e3b996b0427d05441fac2202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\beta) = \\frac{956}{1638} = \\frac{478}{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"38\" />. Through angle addition, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539dfb1a7d9202fff62968a2ebfeb9599c13e1aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(A) = \\frac{478}{525}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. Then, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> can be found given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b00f9945b74c62558a0996749b7c53f201771ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 741$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc0cceb673adfb218b88464ab568d70a7000583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 546$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc569e47dbe14eefc38ba951dad2322f5e65d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{741 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 478}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30ff2a7ce15eeb5ecaf1a4826ff765c32573b36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$478 \\cdot 39^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> minus this area yields the area of the quadrilateral which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494232b440e3006d520d975c7e93b9d8f5ca3e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 13^2 \\cdot 239}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" />. The ration is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738ae78b5a5d63913e2ac4cbc13c8a860c7caa0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 13^2 \\cdot 19 \\cdot 239}{2^4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 13^2 \\cdot 239} \\implies \\boxed{\\mathbf{\\frac{19}{56}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"233\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>To those who say \"The Calculations here are too Big! Who in their right mind would do this??\", students in 2005 are allowed to use calculators during the examination. This was stopped in 2006-07 year.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28For_Educated_Guessing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(For_Educated_Guessing)\">Solution 7 (For Educated Guessing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (For Educated Guessing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69e4c114c34c9b8df57ca40bbf54a69e5a64723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{75}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cadd34099358dd121789838546ad52561cbc6b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> respectively. The numerator being the same on both of the fractions shows that one is probably the correct answer and the other is probably a trick solution.\n</p><p>We can see how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb006087705d18f8a068f3d4e524ad3e351cd2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19+56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69e4c114c34c9b8df57ca40bbf54a69e5a64723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{75}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> is probably there to trick people as it's likely the ratio for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5647cd439ac725d5909d14d188c07cceae22ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{19}{56}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" /> is likely the correct answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A\">2005 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Proble